---
Per-track effect slots currently apply to the master bus, not the track.

User report: assigning FX to Track 3 affects every sound on the mix,
not just Track 3. Source of the bug is in src/engine/mixer.c, where
the existing comment explicitly acknowledges the simplification:

    /* Step 3.5: Per-track insert effects (applied to the mixed output).
     * NOTE: True per-track processing would require separate render buffers
     * per track. For now, we process per-track effects on the master bus
     * when tracks are active — this is a simplification that applies
     * effects to the whole mix, but it lets users assign effects per
     * track in the UI. */

Proper fix requires per-track render buffers. Two possible designs:

1. Tag each voice with its source track_index at trigger time, render
   all voices into separate per-track buffers, apply that track's FX,
   then sum into the master bus.

2. Render each track's voices sequentially into a scratch buffer, apply
   that track's FX, sum into master. Needs a way to filter voices by
   track during rendering (or temporarily deactivate other tracks).

Option 1 is cleaner but touches sampler.c/synth.c/sf2.c render loops.
Option 2 is contained in mixer.c but potentially higher CPU.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Assigning FX to Track 3 affects only Track 3
- [ ] Master FX still affect the full mix
- [ ] No audio glitches from track isolation
- [ ] No heap allocation in the audio path (pre-allocate scratch buffers)
- [ ] Tests: render a pattern with distortion on Track 0 only, assert
      Track 0 has heavy harmonics while Track 1 remains clean

## Test Plan
- [ ] Play a 2-track pattern, put compressor on Track 0 with heavy
      ratio — Track 1 audio should not get ducked
- [ ] Put reverb on every track separately vs on master — output should
      differ noticeably
- [ ] Snapshot test: offline-render output unchanged when no per-track
      FX are active
